import json

def add_v12(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture,link,is_glasses):
 O=P/'engineering-v12-results';c=json.loads((O/'cad_report.json').read_text());m=json.loads((O/'fork_mechanics_summary.json').read_text());s=json.loads((O/'pin_spring_screen.json').read_text());a=json.loads((O/'ocp_motion_audit.json').read_text()) if (O/'ocp_motion_audit.json').exists() else None
 if is_glasses:
  new_page(d,'V12 Shared progress and the Sony pad')
  para(d,'The standalone defender now has six V12 STEP candidates with wider guide channels, an offset fork and a captive folding-lock pin. The independent audit records 216 passing rigid samples and all 18 STEP files pass solid-count and volume checks. V10 remains the latest native Fusion archive. This work does not change the Sony WH CH720N headband or validate a replacement pad.')
  picture(d,'V12_lock_section','Section of the standalone V12 locking mechanism. This is shared project progress, not a proposed change to the Sony headphone. Its integral housing still needs an assembly and servicing design.',5.3)
  para(d,'The standalone child folds give only about 1 to 3 percent reduction in the tight bounding-box volume, so child portability still needs work. The two fork fixtures pass the chosen mesh comparisons, but the complete lock, its cap and fastening design, fatigue and drops are unvalidated. The main Ear Defender Project report contains the full V12 band, pin, spring and failure records.')
  new_page(d,'V12 Replacement pad conclusions remain open')
  table(d,['Question for our Sony pad','Current result','What is needed'],[
   ['Does it fit the mount','Not established','Deferred original pad and groove measurements'],
   ['Does it reduce glasses pressure','Not measured','Original uniform and soft-zone samples at measured host force'],
   ['Does it retain sound isolation','Not measured','Repeated incoming-noise measurements with several frames'],
   ['Does music leak out or change','Not measured','Equal inside-cup playback level outside microphones response and ANC checks'],
   ['Does it stay comfortable in heat','Not measured','Measured foam and cover properties plus warm and humid wear trials'],
   ['Can it last and stay attached','Not measured','Mount retention compression recovery cleaning wear and ageing tests']],[2.05,1.5,3.35])
  para(d,'Our generic V8 replacement cushion and its interface blank are unchanged. No new Sony compatibility, pain-relief, zero-leakage or sound-quality pass has been added. The user owns the headphone and deferred measurements until later; we cannot infer the mounting groove dimensions from the standalone defender.')
  para(d,'The material work still registers 70 families, with limited numerical references and individual foam datapoints. This is not a test of every material formulation. The new V12 pin, spring and band results belong to the standalone mechanism. They do not measure Sony clamp force, cushion compression or cover sealing.')
  para(d,'The first compressed spring-space exports failed a volume check and were replaced with exact cylinders. Coincident fork-copy comparisons also failed; independent located-solid checks and known embedded/disjoint controls are recorded. These failures are retained in the main report and local evidence. Both living reports were updated together on 14 October 2026.')
  para(d,'Affordable Indian supply and a useful glasses zone remain goals. Model-specific measurements and matched original-pad tests come before a benefit claim or a price promise. The market review remains dated 13 October; this engineering update adds no new supplier quote, stock confirmation or competitor test.')
  return
 new_page(d,'V12 Folding lock and wider guides')
 para(d,'V12 adds a folding lock candidate in all six sizes. The fixed tongue has a blind hole. A captive pin in the fork engages this hole in the worn position and pulls back by 6 mm to allow folding. The fork crossbar is offset to clear the new tab. A spring space is reserved inside the housing; it is not an actual coil or a selected production spring.')
 para(d,'The guide to tongue gap increases from about 0.217 mm in V10 to 0.6 mm nominally. Under the same assumed 0.2 mm error on each opposing surface, 0.2 mm clearance remains. This corrects that particular arithmetic shortfall. It does not establish factory capability or clearance with dirt, heat, coatings, misalignment and wear.')
 para(d,'Six local STEP candidates have 32 solids each, including two spring space envelopes. V10 remains the latest native Fusion archive. Fresh band fixture calculations are recorded below when complete. Earlier V10 band stresses and worn-force estimates are not automatically V12 results.')
 picture(d,'V12_lock_candidate','Actual V12 adult small STEP surfaces. Transparent blue shows the fork and housing; green is the tongue and orange is the pin. The two views show engagement and nominal release. The larger assembly is cropped and colours do not specify materials.',6.55)
 if is_glasses:para(d,'This new mechanism belongs to the standalone defender. It does not change the Sony WH CH720N headband or establish pad fit. Our generic replacement cushion still needs the deferred measurements of the Sony mount and physical acoustic comparisons.')
 new_page(d,'V12 Motion checks and CAD reliability')
 para(d,'A positive control exposed a problem in the first motion-check method: two deep geometric copies of the same imported fork returned an empty intersection. A clearance pass from that method alone is not reliable. The original solids pass a separate validity check. The independent OCP audit therefore uses the original geometry with location transforms, avoiding deep geometric copies.')
 if a:
  phases=[('adjustment latched','Slider samples'),('release nominal','Pin release samples'),('folding released','Folding samples')]
  table(d,['Check','Recorded result','Limit'],[[label,str(sum(r['phase']==phase for r in a['cases']))+' samples and '+str(sum(not r['pass'] for r in a['cases'] if r['phase']==phase))+' failures','Rigid discrete positions only'] for phase,label in phases],[1.7,2.15,3.05])
  para(d,'The independent audit covers '+str(a['case_count'])+' poses across six sizes. '+('All recorded poses passed' if a['all_pass'] else 'Some recorded poses failed')+' the 0.01 cubic mm overlap threshold. At each phase start every body pair is considered. Later pairs within the same unchanged rigid group are invariant. Spring envelopes are checked separately. These samples are not a continuous sweep or a loaded contact solution.')
 else:para(d,'The independent OCP motion audit has not completed. No final V12 folding-clearance pass is claimed.')
 para(d,'The first compressed spring-space exports also failed the expected volume check by about 0.994 cubic mm per assembly. Anisotropic dilation had converted the cylindrical surfaces. The revised export reconstructs the annulus from exact cylinders at each length. The initial files and failed checks are kept in the evidence history.')
 k=O/'kernel_controls.json'
 if k.exists():
  k=json.loads(k.read_text());para(d,'The independent collision-query controls include '+str(k['case_count'])+' known embedded and disjoint cube cases, including rotated pairs. '+('They all pass.' if k['all_pass'] else 'Some fail.')+' A one cubic mm cube placed inside a known fork prong must return one cubic mm of overlap; an outside cube must return zero. Coincident independently imported or deeply copied fork comparisons remain unreliable, so no six-size fork-equivalence pass is claimed.')
 para(d,'The lock is still an engineering candidate. The integral housing, large pin collar and head do not yet have a specified assembly or servicing process. A split housing or removable retained cap and head must be designed and checked before manufacturing release. Finger access, pinching, release under load, unintentional unlocking, threads and fastener loosening remain open.')
 pack_path=O/'packing_summary.json'
 if pack_path.exists():
  pack=json.loads(pack_path.read_text());new_page(d,'V12 Folding size and carrying limits')
  table(d,['Size','Folded box mm','Box volume change'],[[r['size'].replace('_',' '),' by '.join(f'{x:.1f}' for x in r['folded_box_mm']),f"{r['reduction_percent']:.1f} percent smaller"] for r in pack['sizes']],[1.6,3.5,1.8])
  para(d,'This comparison uses tight axis-aligned bounding boxes of the actual V12 CAD at its nominal setting and the final sampled fold. The left slider is set to 0 mm and the right to 30 mm before folding. These are space estimates, not a carrying-case measurement or a folded product test.')
  para(d,'The three child examples gain only about 1 to 3 percent in this box-volume measure. Their folded boxes are slightly taller and deeper, so the present child folding arrangement offers little packing benefit. The adult examples gain about 12 to 23 percent. A clear folding path is therefore not enough to call every size easy to carry. Child portability needs further design work and real bag-fit checks.')
  para(d,'These V12 numbers replace any attempt to carry the older V11 packing percentages straight into the new revision. V11 used a different loose bounding-box calculation. Neither study compares a physical market headphone or proves transport survival.')
  if (P/'documents'/'images'/'V12_folded_CAD.png').exists():
   new_page(d,'V12 Nominal and folded CAD')
   picture(d,'V12_folded_CAD','Actual child medium and adult medium STEP surfaces. Nominal and folded views use the same display scale within each row. Triangles are display tessellation, not cover texture. Colours do not select production materials.',6.55)
   para(d,'The child example stays almost the same size in the box-volume comparison. The adult fold gives a clearer packing change. Both still need hand-access, assembly, tolerance, loaded-joint and real carrying-case checks.')
 new_page(d,'V12 Assembly and servicing are still open')
 picture(d,'V12_lock_section','Section curves through the actual saved CAD. The blue housing captures the orange pin collar. This explains nominal retention, but it also shows why we need a defined way to assemble and service the parts. The spring itself is not drawn.',6.55)
 para(d,'The digital pin is captive in the integral housing. We have not specified an economical process for putting the large collar and head inside it, or replacing the spring later. Overmoulding or permanently closing the housing would be a different manufacturing decision, not a tested feature of these CAD files.')
 para(d,'Before ordering a prototype, revise the housing into parts that can be assembled, define a retained cap and pin head, and check their attachment, tolerances, release stroke and folding path. That revised joint must receive its own load analysis. V12 is not released for manufacture.')
 new_page(d,'V12 Fork structural calculations')
 table(d,['Fixture','Fine displacement mm','Fine sampled stress MPa','Mesh change'],[[r['size'].replace('_',' '),f"{r['meshes'][-1]['weighted_load_direction_displacement_mm']:.4f}",f"{r['meshes'][-1]['max_von_mises_centroid_MPa']:.2f}",f"{100*r['displacement_mesh_change_fraction']:.2f} percent displacement and {100*r['sampled_peak_stress_mesh_change_fraction']:.2f} percent stress"] for r in m['cases']],[1.45,1.4,1.4,2.65])
 para(d,'Each fixture uses quadratic tetrahedra with 2.0 and 1.5 mm maximum mesh settings. The adult fine mesh has 103,869 nodes and the child fine mesh has 54,724. Both displacement and sampled peak stress changes pass our chosen 5 percent comparison. The saved equations also pass the residual, force balance, fixed displacement, positive Jacobian and work versus strain-energy checks.')
 para(d,'The input is an illustrative 2 N side load acting through a 65 mm arm. This becomes an 11.63 N resultant at the locking bore. The pivot bore surfaces are fixed and the locking bore receives uniform traction. The material is homogeneous, with an assumed modulus of 2000 MPa and Poisson ratio of 0.35. This is an ideal fork fixture, not the complete pin, tongue, cup and scalp contact system.')
 para(d,'The material comparison has 80 conditional grade and load calculations using ten earlier references at 2, 5, 10 and 20 N. These scale a linear fixture; they are not 80 extra finite-element solves. At 20 N the adult fixture predicts about 132 MPa sampled peak stress. This exceeds the typical yield references of all eight plastics in our table. It is a warning that the present plastic fork cannot receive that load claim from this analysis. Changing to steel is not automatically a solution: weight, processing, interfaces and production grade would need a new design decision.')
 para(d,'A stable mesh comparison is a numerical check. It does not prove a safe overload rating, fracture resistance, fatigue life or drop survival. Corner stresses can still depend on ideal restraints, load distribution and geometry detail. The complete assembled lock still needs its own contact and load analysis. These results apply to the two simulated right-fork examples; they are not automatically six complete assembly results.')
 band_path=O/'band_sizes_summary.json'
 if band_path.exists():
  b=json.loads(band_path.read_text());new_page(d,'V12 Band calculations for the wider guides')
  table(d,['Size','Fine compliance mm per N','Stress mesh change','Chosen comparison'],[[r['size'].replace('_',' '),f"{r['meshes'][-1]['compliance_mm_per_N']:.3f}",f"{100*r['sampled_peak_stress_relative_mesh_change']:.2f} percent",'Pass' if r['chosen_compliance_5percent_gate'] and r['chosen_sampled_peak_stress_5percent_gate'] else 'Fail'] for r in b['cases']],[1.6,1.9,1.7,1.7])
  para(d,'These new calculations use the actual V12 band geometry with wider guide channels in all six sizes. Each is an X half-band with its full front to rear width, the front clamp bore, an illustrative 2 N guide-bottom traction and ideal crown datum restraints. The assumed material remains 2000 MPa with Poisson ratio 0.35. Coarse comparisons that failed are retained and refined rather than renamed as passes.')
  para(d,'The table reports only the last two available mesh comparisons for each size. A passing chosen 5 percent comparison does not bound a local corner stress or prove a finished material or worn headband force. The model omits scalp contact, actual clamp friction, the tongue, cup and folding lock. The earlier V10 equations and physical limits remain in their own revision history.')
 new_page(d,'V12 Pin spring and remaining release work')
 table(d,['Calculation','Result','What it does not prove'],[
 ['Lock pin','36 ideal cases with 2.19 to 2.21 mm pin diameter','Actual bearing, wear, support flexibility or fracture'],
 ['Spring','162 parameter and compression cases','Fatigue, set, buckling, rubbing or reliable return'],
 ['Nominal spring force','About 0.29 N engaged and 0.58 N released','Measured operating force or resistance to accidental release'],
 ['Nominal spring reserve','3.4 mm above solid length when released','Actual end turns, seats and manufacturing variation'],
 ['Pin and bore design limits','0.07 to 0.13 mm diametral clearance','Supplier precision or play after wear']],[1.6,2.35,2.95])
 para(d,'The pin calculation uses an ideal 3.5 mm effective cantilever span. The coil calculation uses 0.35 mm wire, 6 mm mean coil diameter, 14 active turns and 21 mm free length. Published full-hard 301 wire data supply the reference properties. Those wire data do not qualify our final pin, formed coil or heat treatment. Static reference ratios are not fatigue safety factors.')
 link(d,'Published 301 stainless steel wire reference',s['source'])
 para(d,'The remaining work has two parts. Engineering release needs an assembly and retention design, final fasteners and angular stops, complete assembly contact and tolerance checks, and calibrated foam and cover models. Product validation needs manufactured samples for folding cycles, overloads, falls, cleaning, ageing, heat and moisture, measured incoming noise and voluntary comfort feedback. These are not completed tests.')
 para(d,'For the Sony replacement pad, measure the original mount, opening and depth first. Compare original, uniform new and soft-zone samples on the same headphone, with repeated seating and several glasses arms. Incoming sound, outgoing music, bass response and ANC behaviour need real measurements. No zero-leakage, pain-relief, universal preference or market-superiority claim follows from V12.')
 para(d,'Both living Word reports were updated together on 14 October 2026. V12 adds local CAD and component evidence while preserving earlier failures and revision limits. It is not a finished commercial headset or an exhaustive test of every material formulation.')
